{"timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:51:54.222971Z","level":"info","event":"    \"summary_description\": \"<p>The U.S. Department of Energy (DOE)\\u2019s Hydrocarbons and Geothermal Energy Office (HGEO) is issuing this Request for Information (RFI) to notify parties of its potential interest in connecting private capital/ public-private partnership programs to industry opportunities. This initiative provides HGEO\\u2019s technical expertise across the Office of Subsurface Energy\\u2019s three core program areas: Coal, Oil &amp; Gas, and Geothermal. Ultimately, the goal is to use HGEO\\u2019s research and development (R&amp;D) capabilities to support industry and capital.Through this RFI, DOE requests input from all stakeholders, particularly the financial sector, to gauge investor interest in the development and commercialization of subsurface-energy technologies. This is solely a request for information and not a Notice of Funding Opportunity (NOFO). DOE\\u2019s HGEO is not accepting applications for funding at this time.</p>\",","logger":"task.stdout"}
